  "generated_text": "1. **Find the slope of the line:**\n   The slope $m$ of the line passing through the points $(9, 1)$ and $(5, 5)$ is given by:\n   \\[\n   m = \\frac{5 - 1}{5 - 9} = \\frac{4}{-4} = -1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Write the equation of the line:**\n   Using the point-slope form of the equation of a line, we can write the equation of the line passing through $(9, 1)$ with slope $-1$:\n   \\[\n   y - 1 = -1(x - 9)\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   y = -x + 10\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the x-intercept:**\n   To find the x-intercept, set $y = 0$ and solve for $x$:\n   \\[\n   0 = -x + 10 \\implies x = 10\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The line intersects the x-axis at the point $(10, 0)$.\n\n\\boxed{(10,0)}",
  "grade": {
